<p>
  </p><hr>
An example for a program generated with CONVERT is echoo. echoo is similar
to echo, but you can also include binary characters by specifying the hex
code:=20
  <hr>
<pre>@echo off
echo Bj@jzh`0X-`/PPPPPPa(DE(DM(DO(Dh(Ls(Lu(LX(LeZRR]EEEUYRX2Dx=3D&gt;echoo.=
com
echo 0DxFP,0Xx.t0P,=3DXtGsB4o@$?PIyU WwX0GwUY Wv;ovBX2Gv0ExGIuht6&gt;&gt;ec=
hoo.com
echo ?@xAyJHmH@=3Da?}VjuN?_LEkS?`w`s_{OCIvJDGEHtc{OCIKGMgELCI?GGg&gt;&gt;ec=
hoo.com
echo EL?s?WL`LRBcx=3Dk_K?AxVD?fCo?Cd?BLDs0&gt;&gt;echoo.com

echoo This line contains $3c $3e $7c $25 and $24  $0d$0a
echoo           All leading spaces are removed=20
echoo (to get identical results in DOS/Win9x/NT/2000)$0d$0a
echoo $20       insert a explitcit space ($2420) if you want leading spaces=
.=20
del echoo.com
</pre>
<p>
  </p><hr>
